IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part V: reg 89, Social Insurance Numbers.
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering;
-- nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld): reg 89(1), (3), (4) and (6) put duties on the person employed (the Commission, and the employer for (3), (4) and (6),
-- hold the correlative claims); reg 89(2) and (5) put duties on the employer. A duty is encoded twice over, as the rule that says it
-- has arisen and the rule that gives the last day for it; the deadline rules return a DATE and the "in time" rules a BOOLEAN, not a DEONTIC.
-- "Within three days after the day on which the employment begins" ends on that day plus three, and that day counts (the keel's F4).
-- Section 138 of the Act (who must have a Social Insurance Number) is piece ei4's; section 28.1(2) of the Department of Employment and Social
-- Development Act (the register) is outside the two texts.

§ `Regulations Part V - Social Insurance Numbers`

§§ `Reg 89(1) - the person must apply to be registered`

-- Every person employed in insurable employment who is required by s 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number and who has not yet applied
-- to be registered shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, apply to the Commission to be registered.
-- src:1678 | 89 (1) Every person employed in insurable employment who is required by section 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number and who has not yet applied to be registered in the register maintained by the Commission under subsection 28.1(2) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, apply to the Commission to be registered.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(1) (src:1678)
GIVEN `the person is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required by section 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 138 of the Act (piece ei4)
      `the person has not yet applied to be registered in the register maintained by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` IF
        `the person is employed in insurable employment`
    AND `the person is required by section 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number`
    AND `the person has not yet applied to be registered in the register maintained by the Commission`

-- src:1678 | 89 (1) Every person employed in insurable employment who is required by section 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number and who has not yet applied to be registered in the register maintained by the Commission under subsection 28.1(2) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, apply to the Commission to be registered.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(1) (src:1678)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` IS
    `the last day of` 3 `days after` `the day on which the employment begins`

-- src:1678 | 89 (1) Every person employed in insurable employment who is required by section 138 of the Act to have a Social Insurance Number and who has not yet applied to be registered in the register maintained by the Commission under subsection 28.1(2) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, apply to the Commission to be registered.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(1) (src:1678)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person applies to be registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(1) the person applies to be registered within three days after the day on which the employment begins` IF
    `the day on which the person applies to be registered` AT MOST (`reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` `the day on which the employment begins`)

§§ `Reg 89(2) - the employer must ask the employee`

-- An employer who hires a person in insurable employment shall ask the employee, within three days after the day on which the employment begins,
-- to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number.
-- src:1679 | (2) An employer who hires a person in insurable employment shall ask the employee, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(2) (src:1679)
GIVEN `the employer hires the person in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(2) the employer must ask the employee to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` IF
    `the employer hires the person in insurable employment`

-- src:1679 | (2) An employer who hires a person in insurable employment shall ask the employee, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(2) (src:1679)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 89(2) the last day on which the employer must ask the employee` IS
    `the last day of` 3 `days after` `the day on which the employment begins`

-- src:1679 | (2) An employer who hires a person in insurable employment shall ask the employee, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(2) (src:1679)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer asks the employee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(2) the employer asks the employee within three days after the day on which the employment begins` IF
    `the day on which the employer asks the employee` AT MOST (`reg 89(2) the last day on which the employer must ask the employee` `the day on which the employment begins`)

§§ `Reg 89(3) and (4) - the person must inform the employer`

-- (3) Every person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, inform their employer of their number.
-- (4) However, a person who becomes employed before being registered shall inform their employer within three days after the day they receive it.
-- So the last day is the day the employment begins plus three, or, for a person not yet registered when the employment began, the day the number is received plus three
-- (NOTHING while the number has not been received: no time is yet running).
-- src:1680 | (3) Every person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, inform their employer of their Social Insurance Number.
-- src:1681 | (4) However, a person who becomes employed in insurable employment before being registered shall inform their employer of their Social Insurance Number within three days after the day on which they receive it.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(3), reg 89(4) (src:1680-1681)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
      `the person became employed in insurable employment before being registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person receives their Social Insurance Number, if they have` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` IS
    IF `the person became employed in insurable employment before being registered`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day on which the person receives their Social Insurance Number, if they have`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST received THEN JUST (`the last day of` 3 `days after` received)
    ELSE JUST (`the last day of` 3 `days after` `the day on which the employment begins`)

-- src:1680 | (3) Every person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within three days after the day on which the employment begins, inform their employer of their Social Insurance Number.
-- src:1681 | (4) However, a person who becomes employed in insurable employment before being registered shall inform their employer of their Social Insurance Number within three days after the day on which they receive it.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(3), reg 89(4) (src:1680-1681)
GIVEN `the last day on which the person must inform the employer` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person informs the employer, if they have` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` IF
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person informs the employer, if they have`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST informed THEN
        CONSIDER `the last day on which the person must inform the employer`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST lastDay THEN informed AT MOST lastDay

§§ `Reg 89(5) - the employer who cannot ascertain the number must report`

-- An employer who is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall,
-- within six days after the day on which the employment begins, report the matter to the local office of the Commission and provide the information necessary to identify the person.
-- src:1682 | (5) An employer who is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within six days after the day on which the employment begins, report the matter to the local office of the Commission and provide it with the information necessary to identify the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(5) (src:1682)
GIVEN `the employer is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(5) the employer must report the matter to the local office of the Commission` IF
    `the employer is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment`

-- src:1682 | (5) An employer who is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within six days after the day on which the employment begins, report the matter to the local office of the Commission and provide it with the information necessary to identify the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(5) (src:1682)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 89(5) the last day on which the employer must report the matter` IS
    `the last day of` 6 `days after` `the day on which the employment begins`

-- src:1682 | (5) An employer who is unable to ascertain the Social Insurance Number of a person who becomes employed in insurable employment shall, within six days after the day on which the employment begins, report the matter to the local office of the Commission and provide it with the information necessary to identify the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(5) (src:1682)
GIVEN `the day on which the employment begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer reports the matter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(5) the employer reports the matter within six days after the day on which the employment begins` IF
    `the day on which the employer reports the matter` AT MOST (`reg 89(5) the last day on which the employer must report the matter` `the day on which the employment begins`)

§§ `Reg 89(6) - a change in the number or its validity`

-- In the case of a person employed in insurable employment, when the period of their Social Insurance Number validity has been extended, a new period of validity has been assigned
-- to their number, or a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to them, that person shall inform their employer of that change within three days after the day they are informed of it.
-- src:1683 | (6) In the case of a person who is employed in insurable employment, when the period of their Social Insurance Number validity has been extended, a new period of validity has been assigned to their number, or a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to them, that person shall inform their employer of that change within three days after the day on which they are informed of that change.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(6) (src:1683)
GIVEN `the person is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of validity of the person's Social Insurance Number has been extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new period of validity has been assigned to the person's number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` IF
        `the person is employed in insurable employment`
    AND (   `the period of validity of the person's Social Insurance Number has been extended`
         OR `a new period of validity has been assigned to the person's number`
         OR `a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person`)

-- src:1683 | (6) In the case of a person who is employed in insurable employment, when the period of their Social Insurance Number validity has been extended, a new period of validity has been assigned to their number, or a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to them, that person shall inform their employer of that change within three days after the day on which they are informed of that change.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(6) (src:1683)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is informed of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 89(6) the last day on which the person must inform their employer of the change` IS
    `the last day of` 3 `days after` `the day on which the person is informed of the change`

-- src:1683 | (6) In the case of a person who is employed in insurable employment, when the period of their Social Insurance Number validity has been extended, a new period of validity has been assigned to their number, or a new Social Insurance Number has been assigned to them, that person shall inform their employer of that change within three days after the day on which they are informed of that change.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 89(6) (src:1683)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is informed of the change` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person informs their employer of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(6) the person informs their employer of the change within three days after the day they are informed of it` IF
    `the day on which the person informs their employer of the change` AT MOST (`reg 89(6) the last day on which the person must inform their employer of the change` `the day on which the person is informed of the change`)
